{
    "pr_body": "This stops us from applying the `min_doc_count` operation on partial\r\nreduction. If run it on partial reduction then we filter out results\r\nthat might have more docs arrive.\r\n\r\nCloses #89686\r\n",
    "original_commit_id": "4b770d202c402561ea4baa22272e09113ff60090",
    "merged": true,
    "pr_number": 89734,
    "pr_title": "Fix partial reduce bug in ip_prefix",
    "lang": "java",
    "full_name": "elastic/elasticsearch",
    "pr_comment": [
        "Pinging @elastic/es-analytics-geo (Team:Analytics)",
        "Hi @nik9000, I've created a changelog YAML for you.",
        "OK, I see and I understand what is the issue. When we have partial reductions we don't want to filter results based on `min_doc_count` but wait until the final reduction. This way we know how many documents are there in total before filtering based on `min_doc_count`. Otherwise, filtering during partial reduction affects the total number calculated at the end, discarding results that should normally be ok. The following partial reductions might add more documents resulting in a value of doc count that is larger than `min_doc_count`.\r\n\r\nLGTM.",
        "Thanks @salvatore-campagna !"
    ],
    "commit_id": "1f57689218d31a15aa423efbc68cd8ed9e052896",
